{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Claude Sonnet 5 is now available on Amazon Bedrock in AWS GovCloud (US) - AWS","context":"AWS GovCloud (US) has added Claude Sonnet 5 to Amazon Bedrock. This model offers strong performance for coding, professional work, and agentic tasks while balancing capability, cost, and speed. For coding, it handles large codebases, multi-file changes, debugging, and refactoring. For agents, it accurately calls tools, maintains state across steps, and recovers from errors. For knowledge work, it constructs spreadsheets, drafts documents, and converts unstructured data into structured analysis.\n\nClaude Opus 4.8 and Claude Sonnet 5 are now accessible on bedrock-runtime endpoints in US-West and US-East regions of AWS GovCloud (US) and bedrock-mantle endpoints in the US-West region. Bedrock Mantle, Amazon Bedrock's next-generation inference engine, supports the Anthropic Messages API. Amazon Bedrock keeps data within AWS infrastructure and offers access to Claude Sonnet 5 through a unified service with managed features like Guardrails, Knowledge Bases, and regional data residency. For more information, refer to the Amazon Bedrock documentation and regional availability","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/07/claude-sonnet-5-govcloud/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Claude Sonnet 5.5 now available on AWS - AWS","context":"AWS has introduced Claude Sonnet 5.5, an advanced and cost-effective Sonnet for coding and knowledge work. Sonnet 5.5 offers improved efficiency and faster processing compared to Sonnet 5. Customers can access Claude Sonnet 5.5 through two methods: Amazon Bedrock and Claude Platform on AWS. Amazon Bedrock keeps data within AWS infrastructure, offers regional data residency, and includes AWS-managed features like Guardrails and Knowledge Bases. Claude Platform on AWS provides direct access to Anthropic's native platform experience and capabilities via the AWS Console, with unified billing and authentication","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/claude-sonnet-5-5-aws/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"amazon-bedrock","skill_description":"Builds generative AI applications on Amazon Bedrock. Covers model invocation (Converse API, InvokeModel), RAG with Knowledge Bases, Bedrock Agents, Guardrails, and AgentCore (including the Harness managed agent loop). Applies when invoking models, setting up or migrating Knowledge Bases to Managed, deploying to AgentCore, migrating/porting/converting a Bedrock Agent (including inline agents) to an AgentCore Harness, troubleshooting Bedrock errors (ThrottlingException, AccessDeniedException), or choosing Bedrock models (Claude, Llama, Nova, Titan). Also for prompt caching, quota and throttling diagnosis, cost tracking, migrating between Claude model generations, chunking strategies, and Bedrock model selection. Covers AgentCore Payments (x402, microtransactions, Payment Manager, Connector, Instrument, Coinbase CDP, Stripe Privy, paid endpoints, agent payments). NOT for custom model training, Rekognition, or Comprehend. For SageMaker model discovery, customization, or endpoints, use aws-ai-ml.\n\nServices: bedrock, bedrock-runtime, bedrock-mantle, bedrock-agent, bedrock-agent-runtime, bedrock-agentcore-control, bedrock-agentcore\nTasks: deploy, debug, optimize, design, migrate\nPersona: developer, devops, architect\nWorkload: generative-ai, rag, agents","skill_name":"amazon-bedrock"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"Claude Sonnet 4.6 now available in Amazon Bedrock - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock has added support for Claude Sonnet 4.6, a new model from Anthropic. Sonnet 4.6 offers improved performance and reliability for coding, agents, and knowledge work at scale. It is a direct upgrade to Sonnet 4.5 and is suitable for various use cases, including search and chat applications, agentic workflows, and domain-specific applications. The model delivers reliable performance at a lower cost compared to Opus 4.6 intelligence. Developers can use it for multi-model pipelines, and enterprise teams can leverage it for tasks requiring professional precision, such as spreadsheet and financial model creation, compliance review processes, and data summarization. Claude Sonnet 4.6 requires minor prompting adjustments for existing implementations and is now available in Amazon Bedrock. The model is suitable for high-volume deployment and maintains quality standards while optimizing for scale","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/02/claude-sonnet-4.6-available-in-amazon-bedrock/"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"caching-for-llm-inference","skill_description":"Sets up a shared L2 KV cache for self-hosted LLM inference on Amazon ElastiCache for Valkey, so GPU servers load prefill KV state over EFA RDMA instead of recomputing it. Checks fit, estimates savings with KVTrace, builds a business case, creates the cache, connects vLLM or SGLang (also as NVIDIA Dynamo or llm-d workers) through an LMCache server, tunes for cost or latency, and troubleshoots. Use when a builder serves open-weight models on GPUs (for example H100 or B200, on Amazon EC2 or Amazon EKS) for multi-turn chat, agents, RAG, or long contexts and asks about KV cache offloading, prefix cache sharing, prompt caching for self-hosted models, LMCache with Valkey, or lower TTFT or GPU cost. Not for Bedrock prompt caching, LLM response or semantic caching, or general application caching.\n\nServices: elasticache, ec2\nTasks: deploy, optimize, troubleshoot\nPersona: developer, data-scientist, devops\nWorkload: ai-ml","skill_name":"caching-for-llm-inference"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Search docs for Bedrock mantle usage type billing"}

